      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 124,
      "outputTokens": 966,
      "costUsd": 0.008756,
      "pronunciationText": "Once a variable really is uniform, every value carries one over n, so any probability is just ay count. Count the values you want, and divide by n. For a random digit, P of X at least seven counts seven, eight and nine, so it's three tenths. Be careful counting n. Suppose X is uniform on the whole numbers from five to twenty. Twenty minus five is fifteen, but that misses one. Both ends count, so there are sixteen values. Then P of X greater than sixteen counts seventeen, eighteen, nineteen and twenty, which is four sixteenths, or one quarter."
    },
