      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 150,
      "outputTokens": 1084,
      "costUsd": 0.009831000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Two more checks. Say X is uniform on five, ten, fifteen, twenty and twenty-five. P of fifteen is one fifth, because there are five values. It has nothing to do with fifteen being in the middle, or adding up the values. That kind of reasoning would make twenty-five more likely than five, and in a uniform model every value is equally likely. And you can work backwards. If every value has probability zero point zero four, then n is one over zero point zero four, which is twenty-five values. But zero point three can't be the probability of each value, because one over zero point three isn't a whole number. A group of values could still have probability zero point three."
    },
