      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 1000,
      "costUsd": 0.009061,
      "pronunciationText": "One last condition: finitely many values. Watch what happens as the number of equal values grows. Six values, twelve, twenty-four, forty-eight. Each bar is one over n, so the bars get shorter and shorter. Now try infinitely many values, all with the same probability. If that probability is zero, the total is zero. If it's anything bigger than zero, the total passes one once there are enough values. Either way it can't be one. That's why a discrete uniform distribution needs finitely many values. Continuous ones come later, and they work differently."
    },
